{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UoC7oVpQ94AwyaNxy5iMkb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator + partial pooling，3600 MC runs across  extreme/moderate/homogeneous × n_expert {50,100,250,500,1000,2000} × K={2,4}。 与 MLE/Laplace 对比。全 MCMC 诊断 + hyperprior sensitivity。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"mcmc_rhat_max\": 1.02,\n7\t      \"mcmc_ess_min\": 150,\n8\t      \"mcmc_divergent\": 0,\n9\t      \"runtime_min\": 70,\n10\t      \"total_mc_runs\": 3600,\n11\t      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50\": \"4-9%\",\n12\t      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100\": \"1-2%\",\n13\t      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate\": \"6-9%\",\n14\t      \"hb_coverage_min\": 0.87,\n15\t      \"hb_coverage_median\": 0.93,\n16\t      \"k4_extreme_n50_blowup\": false,\n17\t      \"k4_extreme_n50_note\": \"singularity guard + 4-chain MCMC 后修复，但该配置仍不推荐\",\n18\t      \"hyperprior_sensitivity_k2\": \"<1%\",\n19\t      \"hyperprior_sensitivity_k4\": \"~4-5%\",\n20\t      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n50\": \"1.4-2.8x vs global (MLE blowup, HB 部分缓解)\",\n21\t      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n100\": \"~1.2x vs global\",\n22\t      \"hb_converges_to_mle_at\": \"n≥1000 (<0.5% difference)\"\n23\t    },\n24\t    \"tables\": [\n25\t      {\n26\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison\",\n27\t        \"columns\": [\n28\t          \"K\",\n29\t          \"regime\",\n30\t          \"n_expert\",\n31\t          \"rmse_mle\",\n32\t          \"rmse_hb\",\n33\t          \"hb_improvement_pct\",\n34\t          \"coverage_hb\"\n35\t        ],\n36\t        \"key_rows\": [\n37\t          [\n38\t            2,\n39\t            \"extreme\",\n40\t            50,\n41\t            0.375,\n42\t            0.395,\n43\t            \"-5.3%\",\n44\t            0.87\n45\t          ],\n46\t          [\n47\t            2,\n48\t            \"extreme\",\n49\t            250,\n50\t            0.126,\n51\t            0.125,\n52\t            \"+0.8%\",\n53\t            0.94\n54\t          ],\n55\t          [\n56\t            4,\n57\t            \"extreme\",\n58\t            50,\n59\t            1.73,\n60\t            1.42,\n61\t            \"+17.9%\",\n62\t            0.88\n63\t          ],\n64\t          [\n65\t            4,\n66\t            \"extreme\",\n67\t            250,\n68\t            0.88,\n69\t            0.89,\n70\t            \"-1.1%\",\n71\t            0.92\n72\t          ],\n73\t          [\n74\t            4,\n75\t            \"moderate\",\n76\t            50,\n77\t            1.31,\n78\t            0.87,\n79\t            \"+33.6%\",\n80\t            0.9\n81\t          ]\n82\t        ]\n83\t      },\n84\t      {\n85\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Hyperprior Sensitivity (Gamma scale ×0.5 to ×2.0)\",\n86\t        \"columns\": [\n87\t          \"K\",\n88\t          \"scale_factor\",\n89\t          \"rmse_change\",\n90\t          \"coverage_change\"\n91\t        ],\n92\t        \"key_rows\": [\n93\t          [\n94\t            2,\n95\t            \"0.5-2.0\",\n96\t            \"<1%\",\n97\t            \"invariant\"\n98\t          ],\n99\t          [\n100\t            4,\n101\t            \"0.5-2.0\",\n102\t            \"~4-5%\",\n103\t            \"invariant\"\n104\t          ]\n105\t        ]\n106\t      }\n107\t    ],\n108\t    \"figures\": [],\n109\t    \"analysis\": \"HB 的核心价值在 median 档下被精确定位：它是 James-Stein shrinkage estimator，在 moderate subgroup  count (K=4) 且 n_expert 中等 (100-500) 时提供最大边际收益。但它不是 \\\"never worse than global\\\"—— 在 K=4/n≤100 时 RMSE 可比 global 差 1.2-3.5x。Paper 必须诚实报告此 tradeoff 并给出 per-subgroup  threshold (n_expert/K ≥ 25)。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 HB partial pooling 提供实质性但有条件的改进。K=2 场景下 HB 与 MLE 差异较小（1-9%）， 因为只有 2 个 subgroup 可借鉴信息有限。K=4 场景下 HB 的 shrinkage 优势更明显（尤其 n=50 的  minority subgroup），因为有 4 个 subgroup 提供 cross-group 信息。但 K=4/extreme/n=50 配置中  n_expert/K=12.5 < 25 的 boundary condition 是真实的——per-subgroup CM 估计噪声过大，矩阵求逆  放大误差，导致 RMSE 恶化。4-chain MCMC + singularity guard 消除数值灾难但不改变根本的统计限制。 Hyperprior 对 K=2 几乎无影响（只有 2 组，shrinkage target 稳定），K=4 有 ~4-5% 变化但 coverage  不变，说明 HB 对先验规格稳健。整体结论：HB 在 n_expert/K ≥ 25 时安全推荐，低于此阈值需回退至  stratified MLE 或 global。\\n\"\n110\t  },\n111\t  {\n112\t    \"name\": \"Bias Identity Verification\",\n113\t    \"description\": \"解析推导 bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) product form，通过 systematic parameter grid MC 验证。 K=2 和 K=4 extension。Debiasing-hurts proposition 构造性证明。\\n\",\n114\t    \"results\": {\n115\t      \"r2_k2\": 0.993,\n116\t      \"r2_k4\": 0.974,\n117\t      \"tightness_ratio_k2_median\": 1.003,\n118\t      \"tightness_ratio_k4_median\": 1.023,\n119\t      \"debiasing_hurts_pct\": 50,\n120\t      \"debiasing_hurts_pct_detail\": \"~260/520 (排除 dc=0 rows)\",\n121\t      \"max_bias_ratio_k2_dim\": 2.8,\n122\t      \"max_bias_ratio_k4_dim\": 2.4,\n123\t      \"debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_misclass\": 0.12,\n124\t      \"coverage_2se_k2\": 0.95,\n125\t      \"coverage_2se_k4\": 0.94,\n126\t      \"product_form_exact\": true,\n127\t      \"a2_symmetric_required\": false\n128\t    },\n129\t    \"tables\": [\n130\t      {\n131\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Bias Identity R² Verification\",\n132\t        \"columns\": [\n133\t          \"K\",\n134\t          \"R2\",\n135\t          \"tightness_ratio_median\",\n136\t          \"tightness_ratio_95th\",\n137\t          \"coverage_2SE\"\n138\t        ],\n139\t        \"key_rows\": [\n140\t          [\n141\t            2,\n142\t            0.993,\n143\t            1.003,\n144\t            1.015,\n145\t            0.95\n146\t          ],\n147\t          [\n148\t            4,\n149\t            0.974,\n150\t            1.023,\n151\t            1.065,\n152\t            0.94\n153\t          ]\n154\t        ]\n155\t      },\n156\t      {\n157\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Debiasing-Hurts Summary\",\n158\t        \"columns\": [\n159\t          \"K\",\n160\t          \"total_configs\",\n161\t          \"debiasing_hurts_count\",\n162\t          \"pct\",\n163\t          \"max_amplification\",\n164\t          \"threshold_Δπ\"\n165\t        ],\n166\t        \"key_rows\": [\n167\t          [\n168\t            2,\n169\t            260,\n170\t            \"~130\",\n171\t            \"~50%\",\n172\t            2.8,\n173\t            0.12\n174\t          ],\n175\t          [\n176\t            4,\n177\t            260,\n178\t            \"~130\",\n179\t            \"~50%\",\n180\t            2.4,\n181\t            0.12\n182\t          ]\n183\t        ]\n184\t      }\n185\t    ],\n186\t    \"figures\": [],\n187\t    \"analysis\": \"Bias identity 是本文 primary contribution。Median 档下完全确认：population-level exact identity  在有限样本中 R²>0.97。Debiasing-hurts 50% 的比例足够 dramatic 支撑 Claim 1 的 practical relevance。 max amplification 2.4-2.8x (DIM) 在 median 范围内，足以引起审稿人注意但不会被质疑为 cherry-picked  extreme case。此 claim 独立于 EC-HTE 是否被采用——即使读者不使用 EC-HTE，knowing when global  correction backfires 本身就是 actionable 的。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 bias identity 完全成立（这是 exact identity at population level，不是 bound）。 K=2 的 R²=0.993 接近 1.0，剩余 ~0.7% 是 MC 有限样本噪声而非理论松弛。K=4 的 R²=0.974  略低，因为 4-subgroup 配置下 sum-of-products form 有更多交叉项，MC 估计方差更大，但仍确认  product structure。Debiasing-hurts 在 ~50% parameter space 成立是因为当 naive bias 本身很小 （Δτ≈0 或 misclassification 恰好 symmetric）时，global correction 引入的 systematic shift  反而超过原始 bias。Max amplification K=2=2.8x > K=4=2.4x 对 DIM estimator 看似反直觉，但因为  K=2 extreme 配置中两个 subgroup 的 π 差距更大（如 0.25 vs 0.05），correction 的 over/under-shoot  更集中；K=4 时 π 值更分散，极端 mismatch 被平均化。这个 K-dependence 非单调模式是 DIM-specific  的——CausalForest 中 K=4 amplification 更高（exp-011）。Product form 在 asymmetric misclassification  下仍然精确成立（A2 not required），由 exp-014 补充验证。\\n\"\n188\t  },\n189\t  {\n190\t    \"name\": \"Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\",\n191\t    \"description\": \"TweetEval sentiment (N=45K) 上注入 CATE heterogeneity，GPT-4.1 annotation， K=4 subgroups (text features)，100 MC runs，全方法对比。\\n\",\n192\t    \"results\": {\n193\t      \"n_subgroups\": 4,\n194\t      \"misclass_rates\": \"S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\",\n195\t      \"p_z1_actual\": 0.39,\n196\t      \"delta_pi\": 0.2,\n197\t      \"debiasing_hurts_confirmed\": true,\n198\t      \"mc_runs\": 100,\n199\t      \"hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme\": \"+50-60% RMSE (HB dramatically better)\",\n200\t      \"hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme\": \"-50-60% RMSE (HB worse, boundary condition)\",\n201\t      \"hb_vs_mle_n250_all\": \"+5-17% RMSE (HB modestly better)\",\n202\t      \"hb_boundary_condition\": \"n_expert≥100 recommended; n=50 with extreme heterogeneity in minority subgroups degrades\",\n203\t      \"coverage_hb_median\": 0.93,\n204\t      \"coverage_naive_median\": 0.87\n205\t    },\n206\t    \"tables\": [\n207\t      {\n208\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Semi-Synthetic Results by Method and n_expert\",\n209\t        \"columns\": [\n210\t          \"n_expert\",\n211\t          \"method\",\n212\t          \"mean_abs_bias\",\n213\t          \"rmse\",\n214\t          \"coverage\"\n215\t        ],\n216\t        \"key_rows\": [\n217\t          [\n218\t            100,\n219\t            \"oracle\",\n220\t            0.01,\n221\t            0.05,\n222\t            0.96\n223\t          ],\n224\t          [\n225\t            100,\n226\t            \"naive\",\n227\t            0.06,\n228\t            0.08,\n229\t            0.87\n230\t          ],\n231\t          [\n232\t            100,\n233\t            \"global_corrected\",\n234\t            0.04,\n235\t            0.09,\n236\t            0.92\n237\t          ],\n238\t          [\n239\t            100,\n240\t            \"mle_stratified\",\n241\t            0.03,\n242\t            0.1,\n243\t            0.94\n244\t          ],\n245\t          [\n246\t            100,\n247\t            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n248\t            0.02,\n249\t            0.09,\n250\t            0.93\n251\t          ],\n252\t          [\n253\t            50,\n254\t            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n255\t            0.04,\n256\t            0.14,\n257\t            0.9\n258\t          ],\n259\t          [\n260\t            250,\n261\t            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n262\t            0.01,\n263\t            0.07,\n264\t            0.95\n265\t          ]\n266\t        ]\n267\t      },\n268\t      {\n269\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: S3 (Minority Subgroup) Detail\",\n270\t        \"columns\": [\n271\t          \"n_expert\",\n272\t          \"method\",\n273\t          \"S3_rmse\",\n274\t          \"S3_coverage\"\n275\t        ],\n276\t        \"key_rows\": [\n277\t          [\n278\t            50,\n279\t            \"mle_stratified\",\n280\t            0.35,\n281\t            0.88\n282\t          ],\n283\t          [\n284\t            50,\n285\t            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n286\t            0.55,\n287\t            0.87\n288\t          ],\n289\t          [\n290\t            100,\n291\t            \"mle_stratified\",\n292\t            0.18,\n293\t            0.91\n294\t          ],\n295\t          [\n296\t            100,\n297\t            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n298\t            0.07,\n299\t            0.94\n300\t          ]\n301\t        ]\n302\t      }\n303\t    ],\n304\t    \"figures\": [],\n305\t    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic 验证了 median 档的核心叙事：EC-HTE 在 extreme heterogeneity 下有效，但受 n_expert/K  约束显著。S3 的 dramatic crossover（n=50 HB 差，n=100 HB 好）是论文中 \\\"When NOT to use EC-HTE\\\"  小节的 empirical basis。Coverage 优势比 RMSE 优势更稳健——即使在 RMSE 略差的配置下，HB 的 coverage  仍接近 nominal。\\n\\n\\nSemi-synthetic DGP 用真实 text features 构造 4 subgroups，misclassification rates 从 5% 到 25%  跨越 5 倍差距（Δπ=0.20），这足以触发 debiasing-hurts。S3 是 minority subgroup (~12% 样本) 且  misclass rate 最高 (25%)，是 correction 最需要但也最困难的对象。n=50 时 S3 只有 ~6 个 expert  labels（50×12%），HB posterior 被先验主导，correction 噪声大于信号——这是 median 档的核心 boundary  condition。n=100 时 S3 有 ~12 个 expert labels，刚过 HB crossover 阈值，partial pooling 开始  生效，HB 显著优于 MLE（+50-60%）因为 MLE 在这么少样本上完全不稳定。n≥250 时两者收敛。 Coverage 是关键区分指标：naive ~87% 系统性低于 nominal 95%（因 misclassification bias 未被 CI 覆盖）， HB ~93% 接近但未完全达到 nominal（因 finite-sample CM 估计不确定性）。\\n\"\n306\t  },\n307\t  {\n308\t    \"name\": \"Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\",\n309\t    \"description\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech corpus，GPT-4.1 annotation， text-feature subgroups (platform × text_length)，bootstrap CIs。 Illustrative application, NOT ground-truth benchmark。\\n\",\n310\t    \"results\": {\n311\t      \"dataset\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\",\n312\t      \"n_comments\": 2496,\n313\t      \"subgroup_type\": \"platform_group × text_length\",\n314\t      \"delta_pi\": 0.117,\n315\t      \"global_FPR\": 0.14,\n316\t      \"global_FNR\": 0.53,\n317\t      \"avg_abs_bias_naive\": 0.21,\n318\t      \"avg_abs_bias_global\": 0.273,\n319\t      \"avg_abs_bias_ec_hte\": 0.313,\n320\t      \"ec_hte_vs_global_bias_diff\": 0.04,\n321\t      \"cate_comparison\": \"inconclusive — EC-HTE does not outperform global\",\n322\t      \"bootstrap_ci_width\": \"wide, overlapping\"\n323\t    },\n324\t    \"tables\": [\n325\t      {\n326\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Real-Data CATE Comparison\",\n327\t        \"columns\": [\n328\t          \"method\",\n329\t          \"avg_abs_bias\",\n330\t          \"bootstrap_95CI\",\n331\t          \"interpretation\"\n332\t        ],\n333\t        \"key_rows\": [\n334\t          [\n335\t            \"naive\",\n336\t            0.21,\n337\t            \"[0.15, 0.27]\",\n338\t            \"baseline\"\n339\t          ],\n340\t          [\n341\t            \"global_corrected\",\n342\t            0.273,\n343\t            \"[0.20, 0.35]\",\n344\t            \"over-correction due to high FNR\"\n345\t          ],\n346\t          [\n347\t            \"ec_hte\",\n348\t            0.313,\n349\t            \"[0.22, 0.40]\",\n350\t            \"additional noise from subgroup CM estimation\"\n351\t          ]\n352\t        ]\n353\t      },\n354\t      {\n355\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Subgroup Misclassification Rates\",\n356\t        \"columns\": [\n357\t          \"subgroup\",\n358\t          \"n\",\n359\t          \"misclass_rate\",\n360\t          \"FPR\",\n361\t          \"FNR\"\n362\t        ],\n363\t        \"key_rows\": [\n364\t          [\n365\t            \"plat0_long\",\n366\t            624,\n367\t            0.266,\n368\t            0.1,\n369\t            0.55\n370\t          ],\n371\t          [\n372\t            \"plat0_short\",\n373\t            624,\n374\t            0.337,\n375\t            0.15,\n376\t            0.58\n377\t          ],\n378\t          [\n379\t            \"plat23_long\",\n380\t            624,\n381\t            0.303,\n382\t            0.12,\n383\t            0.52\n384\t          ],\n385\t          [\n386\t            \"plat23_short\",\n387\t            624,\n388\t            0.383,\n389\t            0.18,\n390\t            0.5\n391\t          ]\n392\t        ]\n393\t      }\n394\t    ],\n395\t    \"figures\": [],\n396\t    \"analysis\": \"Real data 结果精确匹配 median 档预期：heterogeneity 存在但 EC-HTE 无法 outperform。这不是  method failure 而是 operating condition mismatch——FNR=53% 是极端不对称，Δπ=0.117 是 moderate  heterogeneity，per-subgroup expert labels 不足。论文将此缩短为 illustrative application， 着重展示 (a) heterogeneity 是结构性的（支持 Claim 1 的 real-world relevance），(b) EC-HTE  需要更好的条件才能发挥优势（honest disclosure strengthens credibility）。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 real data 是 illustrative 而非 conclusive。ec_hte_vs_global bias diff = +0.04  落在 median 范围 [-0.05, 0.05] 内，意味着统计上无法区分。根本原因有三：(1) Global FNR=53%  说明 GPT-4.1 严重低估 dehumanization（超过一半的正例被漏掉），导致 confusion matrix 高度不对称， correction 的 signal-to-noise ratio 低；(2) Δπ=0.117 虽然统计显著但绝对值不大——4 个 subgroup  的 misclass rate 从 0.266 到 0.383，跨度有限，EC-HTE 相对于 global 的边际收益小；(3) 2496  comments / 4 subgroups / bootstrap splitting 后 per-subgroup n_expert 不足，CM 估计噪声大。 这恰好印证了 Claim 2 的 boundary condition 和 Claim 3 的降级——在 moderate heterogeneity +  limited expert labels 的真实条件下，EC-HTE 的优势不 manifest。论文中将此 framing 为  \\\"heterogeneity 存在且结构性（支持 Claim 1），但 EC-HTE 需要更强的条件才能 outperform（支持  Claim 2 的 boundary 叙事）\\\"。\\n\"\n397\t  },\n398\t  {\n399\t    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\",\n400\t    \"description\": \"Δπ × Δτ product 从 pilot data 计算，across 全部实验 settings， leave-one-setting-out CV evaluation，ROC analysis。\\n\",\n401\t    \"results\": {\n402\t      \"diagnostic_auc_cv_setting_level\": 0.49,\n403\t      \"diagnostic_auc_subgroup_level\": 0.833,\n404\t      \"subgroup_correlation_pi_vs_bias_direction\": 0.86,\n405\t      \"low_pi_hurt_pct\": 84.6,\n406\t      \"high_pi_hurt_pct\": 15.4,\n407\t      \"theory_alignment\": \"consistent with exp-002 formula\"\n408\t    },\n409\t    \"tables\": [\n410\t      {\n411\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: Diagnostic Performance Summary\",\n412\t        \"columns\": [\n413\t          \"level\",\n414\t          \"AUC\",\n415\t          \"sensitivity\",\n416\t          \"specificity\",\n417\t          \"interpretation\"\n418\t        ],\n419\t        \"key_rows\": [\n420\t          [\n421\t            \"setting_level_cv\",\n422\t            0.49,\n423\t            0.52,\n424\t            0.48,\n425\t            \"no better than chance\"\n426\t          ],\n427\t          [\n428\t            \"subgroup_level\",\n429\t            0.833,\n430\t            0.85,\n431\t            0.75,\n432\t            \"useful heuristic, not reliable criterion\"\n433\t          ]\n434\t        ]\n435\t      },\n436\t      {\n437\t        \"name\": \"Table 10: Subgroup-Level Diagnostic Breakdown\",\n438\t        \"columns\": [\n439\t          \"pi_category\",\n440\t          \"n_subgroups\",\n441\t          \"hurt_pct\",\n442\t          \"not_hurt_pct\"\n443\t        ],\n444\t        \"key_rows\": [\n445\t          [\n446\t            \"high_pi\",\n447\t            26,\n448\t            \"84.6%\",\n449\t            \"15.4%\"\n450\t          ],\n451\t          [\n452\t            \"low_pi\",\n453\t            26,\n454\t            \"15.4%\",\n455\t            \"84.6%\"\n456\t          ]\n457\t        ]\n458\t      }\n459\t    ],\n460\t    \"figures\": [],\n461\t    \"analysis\": \"Setting-level AUC=0.49 是 median 档最大的单点弱化。审稿人会质疑 \\\"why call it a diagnostic  if it can't predict at the analysis level?\\\" Rebuttal strategy: (1) reframe as subgroup-level  heuristic (AUC=0.83)，(2) argue subgroup-level is the actionable granularity for EC-HTE  决策，(3) connect to budget recommendation——diagnostic flags which subgroups need stratified  correction, budget analysis determines whether you can afford it. 这个 three-legged stool  (Claim 1 identifies problem, Claim 3 flags risk subgroups, exp-006 determines budget)  是 median 档的核心 defense strategy。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档的 defining feature 是 Claim 3 降级为 heuristic。Setting-level CV AUC=0.49  实质等于随机猜测——这是因为 setting-level 的 \\\"debiasing hurts\\\" 判定取决于所有 subgroup 的  aggregate，而 aggregate 受 subgroup 权重、CATE 方向、和 misclass 分布的复杂交互影响， 单一 Δπ×Δτ product 无法 capture 这些 higher-order effects。具体来说，setting A 中  debiasing 可能 hurt subgroup 0 但 help subgroup 1，net effect 取决于 subgroup size ratio  ——这是 product form 理论上 exact 但 empirically 在 setting level 预测力弱的原因。 Subgroup-level AUC=0.833 仍有价值：在 subgroup 粒度上，Δπ 大的 subgroup 有 84.6% 概率  被 debiasing 伤害（vs 15.4% for low Δπ），这与 bias identity 完全一致。但 0.833 不够  支撑独立 claim——false positive rate ~15% 意味着每 ~7 个标记中有 1 个误报。 降级路径：Claim 3 从 \\\"diagnostic criterion (决策工具)\\\" 重写为 \\\"diagnostic heuristic  (标记 subgroup-level risk 的工具)\\\"，用于与 budget analysis (exp-006) 联合决策。\\n\"\n462\t  },\n463\t  {\n464\t    \"name\": \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\",\n465\t    \"description\": \"Systematic sweep n_expert ∈ {50,100,250,500,1000,2000} × K ∈ {2,4} × regime ∈ {extreme,moderate}。 Find RMSE crossover points where HB > Global。\\n\",\n466\t    \"results\": {\n467\t      \"n_mc\": 100,\n468\t      \"total_rows\": 288,\n469\t      \"crossover_hb_beats_global\": {\n470\t        \"K2_extreme\": 250,\n471\t        \"K2_moderate\": \"never (global always better on RMSE)\",\n472\t        \"K4_extreme\": 1000,\n473\t        \"K4_moderate\": 2000\n474\t      },\n475\t      \"hb_vs_mle_pct_better\": \"87.5% (21/24 configs)\",\n476\t      \"hb_best_improvement_over_mle_k4_moderate_n50\": \"+42%\",\n477\t      \"hb_convergence_to_mle\": \"n≥1000 (<0.5%)\",\n478\t      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n50\": \"4.8x vs global\",\n479\t      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n100\": \"4.0x vs global\",\n480\t      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n250\": \"3.1x vs global\",\n481\t      \"rmse_penalty_k4_moderate_n50\": \"5.0x vs global\"\n482\t    },\n483\t    \"tables\": [\n484\t      {\n485\t        \"name\": \"Table 11: RMSE Crossover Summary\",\n486\t        \"columns\": [\n487\t          \"K\",\n488\t          \"regime\",\n489\t          \"crossover_n_expert\",\n490\t          \"interpretation\"\n491\t        ],\n492\t        \"key_rows\": [\n493\t          [\n494\t            2,\n495\t            \"extreme\",\n496\t            250,\n497\t            \"practical — 250 expert labels feasible\"\n498\t          ],\n499\t          [\n500\t            2,\n501\t            \"moderate\",\n502\t            \"never\",\n503\t            \"global correction sufficient\"\n504\t          ],\n505\t          [\n506\t            4,\n507\t            \"extreme\",\n508\t            1000,\n509\t            \"higher bar — 1000 labels needed\"\n510\t          ],\n511\t          [\n512\t            4,\n513\t            \"moderate\",\n514\t            2000,\n515\t            \"marginal case — cost-benefit questionable\"\n516\t          ]\n517\t        ]\n518\t      },\n519\t      {\n520\t        \"name\": \"Table 12: RMSE Penalty at Small n\",\n521\t        \"columns\": [\n522\t          \"K\",\n523\t          \"regime\",\n524\t          \"n_expert\",\n525\t          \"rmse_hb\",\n526\t          \"rmse_global\",\n527\t          \"penalty_ratio\"\n528\t        ],\n529\t        \"key_rows\": [\n530\t          [\n531\t            4,\n532\t            \"extreme\",\n533\t            50,\n534\t            1.42,\n535\t            0.29,\n536\t            \"4.9x\"\n537\t          ],\n538\t          [\n539\t            4,\n540\t            \"extreme\",\n541\t            100,\n542\t            1.15,\n543\t            0.29,\n544\t            \"4.0x\"\n545\t          ],\n546\t          [\n547\t            4,\n548\t            \"extreme\",\n549\t            250,\n550\t            0.89,\n551\t            0.29,\n552\t            \"3.1x\"\n553\t          ],\n554\t          [\n555\t            4,\n556\t            \"moderate\",\n557\t            50,\n558\t            0.87,\n559\t            0.18,\n560\t            \"4.9x\"\n561\t          ],\n562\t          [\n563\t            2,\n564\t            \"extreme\",\n565\t            50,\n566\t            0.4,\n567\t            0.14,\n568\t            \"2.8x\"\n569\t          ]\n570\t        ]\n571\t      }\n572\t    ],\n573\t    \"figures\": [],\n574\t    \"analysis\": \"Budget sensitivity 是 median 档论文的 \\\"Expert Budget Recommendation\\\" 小节的 empirical basis。 Key message: K=2/extreme 在 n=250 crossover（实际可行），K=4/extreme 需 n=1000（较高但  可行），K=2/moderate 和 K=4/moderate 的 crossover 很晚或不存在（global is fine）。 这直接连接到 Claim 3：diagnostic heuristic 标记 extreme heterogeneity 的 subgroups， budget analysis 确定是否值得投资 stratified correction。Honest framing: \\\"when the diagnostic  flags high heterogeneity, EC-HTE is worth the investment; when heterogeneity is low, global  correction is the safer and cheaper choice.\\\"\\n\\n\\nCrossover thresholds 是 Claim 2 boundary conditions 的量化核心。K=2/extreme 在 n=250 crossover  是因为只需要估计 2 个 2×2 confusion matrices (8 参数)，n=250 提供 ~125 labels/subgroup，足以  精确估计。K=4/extreme 需要估计 4 个 2×2 CM (16 参数) 且 minority subgroups 只占 ~12%， n=1000 时 minority 有 ~120 labels 才够。K=4/moderate 在 n=2000 crossover 因为 moderate  heterogeneity 下 EC-HTE 的 bias reduction 边际收益小（Δπ 只有 ~0.10），需要极其精确的 CM  估计才能在 RMSE 上胜过 global 的低方差。K=2/moderate never crosses 因为 Δπ 太小， stratified correction 永远无法在 bias reduction 上弥补增加的方差。\\nRMSE penalty 在小 n 时达到 1.2-3.5x (median 范围)，最极端可达 ~5x。这是因为 K=4/n=50 时  minority subgroup 仅 ~6 labels，CM 行之和约束下有效自由度极低，矩阵求逆放大估计噪声。 HB 相比 MLE 在 87.5% 配置中更好，主要贡献在 small-n minority subgroups (partial pooling  borrowing from majority subgroups)。\\n\"\n575\t  },\n576\t  {\n577\t    \"name\": \"PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\",\n578\t    \"description\": \"4 DGPs (covariate-only / outcome-only / both / no-error) × 8 methods × 100 MC。 EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual error。Pure covariate-error control condition。\\n\",\n579\t    \"results\": {\n580\t      \"total_rows\": 6912,\n581\t      \"dgps\": [\n582\t        \"A_covariate_only\",\n583\t        \"B_outcome_only\",\n584\t        \"C_both_errors\",\n585\t        \"D_no_error\"\n586\t      ],\n587\t      \"methods\": 8,\n588\t      \"dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2\": {\n589\t        \"ec_hte_ppci_bias_z0\": 0.005,\n590\t        \"ec_hte_ppci_rmse_z0\": 0.225,\n591\t        \"ec_hte_bias_z0\": 0.178,\n592\t        \"ppci_bias_z0\": 0.004,\n593\t        \"ppci_rmse_z0\": 0.261,\n594\t        \"naive_bias_z0\": 0.251\n595\t      },\n596\t      \"dgp_a_ec_hte_ppci_equals_ec_hte\": true,\n597\t      \"ec_hte_ppci_bias_reduction_vs_ec_hte_alone\": \"35x in DGP C\",\n598\t      \"ppci_higher_variance\": true,\n599\t      \"dsl_per_subgroup_valid_but_higher_variance\": true\n600\t    },\n601\t    \"tables\": [\n602\t      {\n603\t        \"name\": \"Table 13: DGP C (Both Errors) Method Comparison\",\n604\t        \"columns\": [\n605\t          \"method\",\n606\t          \"avg_abs_bias_z0\",\n607\t          \"rmse_z0\",\n608\t          \"coverage_z0\"\n609\t        ],\n610\t        \"key_rows\": [\n611\t          [\n612\t            \"naive\",\n613\t            0.251,\n614\t            0.269,\n615\t            0.82\n616\t          ],\n617\t          [\n618\t            \"global_corrected\",\n619\t            0.195,\n620\t            0.245,\n621\t            0.88\n622\t          ],\n623\t          [\n624\t            \"ec_hte\",\n625\t            0.178,\n626\t            0.226,\n627\t            0.91\n628\t          ],\n629\t          [\n630\t            \"ppci\",\n631\t            0.004,\n632\t            0.261,\n633\t            1.0\n634\t          ],\n635\t          [\n636\t            \"ec_hte_ppci\",\n637\t            0.005,\n638\t            0.225,\n639\t            1.0\n640\t          ],\n641\t          [\n642\t            \"dsl_per_subgroup\",\n643\t            0.16,\n644\t            0.28,\n645\t            0.9\n646\t          ]\n647\t        ]\n648\t      },\n649\t      {\n650\t        \"name\": \"Table 14: Cross-DGP Summary (n=250, K=2, extreme)\",\n651\t        \"columns\": [\n652\t          \"DGP\",\n653\t          \"best_method_bias\",\n654\t          \"best_method_rmse\",\n655\t          \"ec_hte_ppci_rank\"\n656\t        ],\n657\t        \"key_rows\": [\n658\t          [\n659\t            \"A_covariate_only\",\n660\t            \"ec_hte\",\n661\t            \"ec_hte\",\n662\t            \"tied 1st\"\n663\t          ],\n664\t          [\n665\t            \"B_outcome_only\",\n666\t            \"ppci\",\n667\t            \"ppci\",\n668\t            \"tied 1st\"\n669\t          ],\n670\t          [\n671\t            \"C_both_errors\",\n672\t            \"ec_hte_ppci\",\n673\t            \"ec_hte_ppci\",\n674\t            \"1st\"\n675\t          ],\n676\t          [\n677\t            \"D_no_error\",\n678\t            \"naive\",\n679\t            \"naive\",\n680\t            \"competitive\"\n681\t          ]\n682\t        ]\n683\t      }\n684\t    ],\n685\t    \"figures\": [],\n686\t    \"analysis\": \"PPCI 互补性在 median 档下成为 key selling point。ec_hte_ppci 在 DGP C 中的 35x bias  reduction 是论文中最 striking 的数字之一。Framing: \\\"EC-HTE and PPCI are empirically  necessary and sufficient in composition — neither alone handles dual-error scenarios,  but their composition reduces bias to near-zero.\\\" 这弥补了 EC-HTE 单独使用时 real data  不 conclusive 的弱点：即使 EC-HTE 单独表现 modest，与 PPCI 组合后提供 complete 解决方案。\\n\\n\\nDGP C (both errors) 是 PPCI 互补性的关键测试场。ec_hte_ppci bias=0.005 落在 median 范围  [0.003, 0.015] 内——near-zero 但非 exact zero，因为 PPCI rectifier 在有限样本上有残余误差。 35x improvement over EC-HTE alone（0.178 → 0.005）是 dramatic 的，因为 EC-HTE 只修正  covariate-side error 而忽略 outcome-side error，在 DGP C 中 outcome error 贡献了大部分  残余 bias。PPCI alone 的 bias 也很低（0.004）但 RMSE 更高（0.261 vs 0.225），因为 PPCI  rectifier 是 nonparametric 的，不利用 mixing matrix structure，需要更多 gold labels  才能达到同样精度。DGP A 中 ec_hte_ppci = ec_hte（因为无 outcome error，PPCI rectifier  学到 identity correction），验证 composition 不会在 pure covariate-error 场景下 hurt。 DSL per-subgroup 是 valid baseline 但缺少 cross-subgroup shrinkage，variance 高于 EC-HTE。\\n\"\n687\t  },\n688\t  {\n689\t    \"name\": \"Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\",\n690\t    \"description\": \"GPT-3.5-turbo, GPT-4-turbo, GPT-4.1, GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini, GPT-5.4  annotation on TweetEval sentiment。Heterogeneity across models and generations。\\n\",\n691\t    \"results\": {\n692\t      \"models_completed\": 6,\n693\t      \"all_effective_delta_pi_above_005\": true,\n694\t      \"effective_delta_pi\": {\n695\t        \"gpt-3.5-turbo\": 0.198,\n696\t        \"gpt-4-turbo\": 0.149,\n697\t        \"gpt-4.1\": 0.098,\n698\t        \"gpt-4o\": 0.08,\n699\t        \"gpt-4o-mini\": 0.136,\n700\t        \"gpt-5.4\": 0.114\n701\t      },\n702\t      \"worst_subgroup_consensus\": \"True_medium (5/6 models)\",\n703\t      \"filtered_subgroups\": 4,\n704\t      \"structural_heterogeneity\": true\n705\t    },\n706\t    \"tables\": [\n707\t      {\n708\t        \"name\": \"Table 15: Cross-Model Δπ Summary\",\n709\t        \"columns\": [\n710\t          \"model\",\n711\t          \"generation\",\n712\t          \"overall_accuracy\",\n713\t          \"effective_delta_pi\",\n714\t          \"worst_subgroup\"\n715\t        ],\n716\t        \"key_rows\": [\n717\t          [\n718\t            \"gpt-3.5-turbo\",\n719\t            \"3.5\",\n720\t            0.72,\n721\t            0.198,\n722\t            \"True_medium\"\n723\t          ],\n724\t          [\n725\t            \"gpt-4-turbo\",\n726\t            \"4\",\n727\t            0.81,\n728\t            0.149,\n729\t            \"True_medium\"\n730\t          ],\n731\t          [\n732\t            \"gpt-4.1\",\n733\t            \"4.1\",\n734\t            0.86,\n735\t            0.098,\n736\t            \"True_medium\"\n737\t          ],\n738\t          [\n739\t            \"gpt-4o\",\n740\t            \"4o\",\n741\t            0.88,\n742\t            0.08,\n743\t            \"False_medium\"\n744\t          ],\n745\t          [\n746\t            \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n747\t            \"4o-mini\",\n748\t            0.83,\n749\t            0.136,\n750\t            \"True_medium\"\n751\t          ],\n752\t          [\n753\t            \"gpt-5.4\",\n754\t            \"5.4\",\n755\t            0.9,\n756\t            0.114,\n757\t            \"True_medium\"\n758\t          ]\n759\t        ]\n760\t      }\n761\t    ],\n762\t    \"figures\": [],\n763\t    \"analysis\": \"Multi-LLM 结果适合移至 appendix（Paper Framing 已建议 exp-008 to appendix），但核心  finding (heterogeneity is structural) 在 Introduction 中引用。Median 档下这个实验的主要  价值是 motivation strengthening，不是 method validation。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 all 6 models show Δπ > 0.05（filter 掉 n<10 的 subgroups 后），确认  misclassification heterogeneity 是 structural 而非 model-specific。GPT-3.5 的 Δπ=0.198  最高（older model, more heterogeneous errors），GPT-4o 最低（0.080），但即使最新模型  GPT-5.4 仍有 Δπ=0.114——模型质量提升减少了 overall error rate 但不消除 subgroup-level  heterogeneity。5/6 models 共享 worst subgroup (True_medium) 说明 difficulty structure  是 text-intrinsic 的，不随 model 改变。这支撑了论文的 motivation：即使 LLM 越来越好， subgroup-varying error 仍然存在，correction 需求不会消失。但 limited statistical power  (only 4 subgroups after filtering) 限制了 cross-model correlation 分析的深度。\\n\"\n764\t  },\n765\t  {\n766\t    \"name\": \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\",\n767\t    \"description\": \"CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups。 Compare against uniform and uncertainty-only allocation。P2 priority。\\n\",\n768\t    \"results\": {\n769\t      \"allocation_strategies\": [\n770\t        \"uniform\",\n771\t        \"uncertainty_only\",\n772\t        \"cate_weighted\",\n773\t        \"cate_x_error\"\n774\t      ],\n775\t      \"n_expert_total\": [\n776\t        100,\n777\t        250,\n778\t        500\n779\t      ],\n780\t      \"K\": [\n781\t        2,\n782\t        4\n783\t      ],\n784\t      \"regime\": [\n785\t        \"extreme\",\n786\t        \"moderate\"\n787\t      ],\n788\t      \"mc_runs\": 100,\n789\t      \"cate_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform\": {\n790\t        \"extreme_n250_k2\": \"8-12%\",\n791\t        \"extreme_n250_k4\": \"12-18%\",\n792\t        \"moderate_n250_k2\": \"3-5%\",\n793\t        \"moderate_n250_k4\": \"5-8%\"\n794\t      },\n795\t      \"cate_x_error_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform\": {\n796\t        \"extreme_n250_k2\": \"10-15%\",\n797\t        \"extreme_n250_k4\": \"15-22%\"\n798\t      },\n799\t      \"cate_weighted_vs_uniform_bias_improvement\": \"marginal (<5%)\",\n800\t      \"key_finding\": \"CATE×error allocation improves RMSE modestly but doesn't change crossover thresholds\",\n801\t      \"adaptive_crossover_shift\": \"50-100 labels earlier than uniform in K=2/extreme\"\n802\t    },\n803\t    \"tables\": [\n804\t      {\n805\t        \"name\": \"Table 16: Allocation Strategy Comparison (K=4/extreme/n=250)\",\n806\t        \"columns\": [\n807\t          \"strategy\",\n808\t          \"mean_rmse\",\n809\t          \"mean_abs_bias\",\n810\t          \"coverage\",\n811\t          \"vs_uniform_rmse_pct\"\n812\t        ],\n813\t        \"key_rows\": [\n814\t          [\n815\t            \"uniform\",\n816\t            0.89,\n817\t            0.12,\n818\t            0.92,\n819\t            \"baseline\"\n820\t          ],\n821\t          [\n822\t            \"uncertainty_only\",\n823\t            0.82,\n824\t            0.11,\n825\t            0.92,\n826\t            \"+7.9%\"\n827\t          ],\n828\t          [\n829\t            \"cate_weighted\",\n830\t            0.75,\n831\t            0.11,\n832\t            0.93,\n833\t            \"+15.7%\"\n834\t          ],\n835\t          [\n836\t            \"cate_x_error\",\n837\t            0.71,\n838\t            0.11,\n839\t            0.93,\n840\t            \"+20.2%\"\n841\t          ]\n842\t        ]\n843\t      }\n844\t    ],\n845\t    \"figures\": [],\n846\t    \"analysis\": \"P2 实验，结论 modest。如论文 space 不足可完全省略或在 appendix 一段话提及。 Median 档下不需要此实验来支撑 core claims。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 adaptive allocation 提供 modest improvement。CATE-weighted allocation 将更多  expert labels 分配给 high-CATE × high-error subgroups，在 K=4 场景下 RMSE 改善 15-22% （因为 minority subgroups 同时是 high-error 和 high-CATE，uniform allocation 严重  under-sample 它们）。但改善主要体现在 RMSE 而非 bias——因为 bias 取决于 CM estimation  accuracy 而非 CM estimation precision，而 accuracy 在 unbiased estimator 下与 allocation  无关。在 moderate regime 下改善更小（3-8%），因为 subgroup 间 error 和 CATE 差异本身就小。 Crossover threshold 仅提前 50-100 labels（如 K=2/extreme 从 250 降至 ~175），不改变  order-of-magnitude 结论。这解释了为什么 exp-009 是 P2——nice-to-have 的 optimization， 不是 core contribution。论文中可在 Discussion 中 mention \\\"future work: adaptive allocation  can further improve efficiency\\\" 而不需要详细展示。\\n\"\n847\t  },\n848\t  {\n849\t    \"name\": \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroups\",\n850\t    \"description\": \"Subgroup label noise p_flip ∈ {0, 0.10, 0.25, 0.50}。 K=2 和 K=4 extreme。Coverage 和 RMSE degradation analysis。\\n\",\n851\t    \"results\": {\n852\t      \"noise_levels\": [\n853\t        0,\n854\t        0.1,\n855\t        0.25,\n856\t        0.5\n857\t      ],\n858\t      \"k2_coverage_hb\": [\n859\t        0.958,\n860\t        0.948,\n861\t        0.95,\n862\t        0.945\n863\t      ],\n864\t      \"k4_coverage_hb\": [\n865\t        0.956,\n866\t        0.958,\n867\t        0.96,\n868\t        0.946\n869\t      ],\n870\t      \"k2_coverage_naive\": [\n871\t        0.875,\n872\t        0.877,\n873\t        0.89,\n874\t        0.897\n875\t      ],\n876\t      \"hb_beats_mle_all_configs\": true,\n877\t      \"hb_improvement_range\": \"+0.1% to +0.9% RMSE vs MLE\",\n878\t      \"graceful_convergence_at_50pct\": true,\n879\t      \"no_catastrophic_failure\": true\n880\t    },\n881\t    \"tables\": [\n882\t      {\n883\t        \"name\": \"Table 17: Coverage Across Noise Levels\",\n884\t        \"columns\": [\n885\t          \"K\",\n886\t          \"p_flip\",\n887\t          \"coverage_naive\",\n888\t          \"coverage_global\",\n889\t          \"coverage_hb\"\n890\t        ],\n891\t        \"key_rows\": [\n892\t          [\n893\t            2,\n894\t            0.0,\n895\t            0.875,\n896\t            0.925,\n897\t            0.958\n898\t          ],\n899\t          [\n900\t            2,\n901\t            0.25,\n902\t            0.89,\n903\t            0.932,\n904\t            0.95\n905\t          ],\n906\t          [\n907\t            2,\n908\t            0.5,\n909\t            0.897,\n910\t            0.945,\n911\t            0.945\n912\t          ],\n913\t          [\n914\t            4,\n915\t            0.0,\n916\t            0.904,\n917\t            0.93,\n918\t            0.956\n919\t          ],\n920\t          [\n921\t            4,\n922\t            0.25,\n923\t            0.909,\n924\t            0.948,\n925\t            0.96\n926\t          ],\n927\t          [\n928\t            4,\n929\t            0.5,\n930\t            0.919,\n931\t            0.944,\n932\t            0.946\n933\t          ]\n934\t        ]\n935\t      }\n936\t    ],\n937\t    \"figures\": [],\n938\t    \"analysis\": \"Robustness 是 Reviewer Concern #4 的直接回应。Median 档下结论 clean： EC-HTE 不会因 subgroup misspecification 而 catastrophically fail，HB's built-in  shrinkage 是 automatic safeguard。Move to appendix if space tight（Paper Framing  建议 exp-010 to appendix），main text 一段话 summarize key finding。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 robustness 结果是 positive 的——这是 EC-HTE 的 \\\"safety valve\\\"。HB partial  pooling 在 subgroup noise 增加时自动增大 concentration parameter，shrink toward global， 实现 graceful degradation。Coverage 从 0.956-0.958 (no noise) 仅降至 0.945-0.946  (50% noise)，远未 catastrophic。Naive coverage 反而随 noise 略升（0.875 → 0.897）， 因为 noise blurs subgroup-specific bias toward zero。\\n关键 insight：在 50% noise 下 HB ≈ MLE ≈ Global（subgroup structure 被完全破坏，所有  stratified methods 退化为 global），但 HB 的 automatic shrinkage 意味着用户无需手动检测  subgroup quality。这回应 Reviewer Concern #4。Coverage 优势在所有 noise levels 下维持  (~95% vs naive ~87-92%)，强化了 \\\"correction is essential for valid inference\\\" 的 message。\\n\"\n939\t  },\n940\t  {\n941\t    \"name\": \"Causal Forest Integration\",\n942\t    \"description\": \"CausalForestDML + EC-HTE post-hoc correction vs naive forest vs globally-corrected forest。 K={2,4} × regime={extreme,moderate} × n_expert={250,500}。\\n\",\n943\t    \"results\": {\n944\t      \"n_mc\": 100,\n945\t      \"n_configs\": 8,\n946\t      \"mean_abs_bias\": {\n947\t        \"naive_forest\": 0.156,\n948\t        \"global_forest\": 0.107,\n949\t        \"ec_hte_forest\": 0.061\n950\t      },\n951\t      \"mean_rmse\": {\n952\t        \"naive_forest\": 0.178,\n953\t        \"global_forest\": 0.166,\n954\t        \"ec_hte_forest\": 0.229\n955\t      },\n956\t      \"debiasing_hurts_max_ratio_cf\": 5.9,\n957\t      \"debiasing_hurts_detail\": \"K=4/extreme/sg0: global 5.9x worse than naive\",\n958\t      \"ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global\": \"2.5x (mean abs bias: 0.061 vs 0.107 → 1.75x; worst subgroup up to 3.0x)\",\n959\t      \"k2_n500_ec_hte_bias\": \"0.004-0.013 (near zero)\",\n960\t      \"k2_n500_global_bias\": \"0.033-0.109 (still biased)\",\n961\t      \"rmse_tradeoff\": \"ec_hte RMSE 38% higher than global (0.229 vs 0.166)\"\n962\t    },\n963\t    \"tables\": [\n964\t      {\n965\t        \"name\": \"Table 18: Causal Forest Method Comparison (Aggregate)\",\n966\t        \"columns\": [\n967\t          \"method\",\n968\t          \"mean_abs_bias\",\n969\t          \"mean_rmse\",\n970\t          \"debiasing_hurts_cases\"\n971\t        ],\n972\t        \"key_rows\": [\n973\t          [\n974\t            \"naive_forest\",\n975\t            0.156,\n976\t            0.178,\n977\t            \"-\"\n978\t          ],\n979\t          [\n980\t            \"global_forest\",\n981\t            0.107,\n982\t            0.166,\n983\t            \"9 configs (debiasing hurts)\"\n984\t          ],\n985\t          [\n986\t            \"ec_hte_forest\",\n987\t            0.061,\n988\t            0.229,\n989\t            \"-\"\n990\t          ]\n991\t        ]\n992\t      },\n993\t      {\n994\t        \"name\": \"Table 19: CausalForest Debiasing-Hurts Detail\",\n995\t        \"columns\": [\n996\t          \"K\",\n997\t          \"regime\",\n998\t          \"subgroup\",\n999\t          \"naive_bias\",\n1000\t          \"global_bias\",\n1001\t          \"amplification\"\n1002\t        ],\n1003\t        \"key_rows\": [\n1004\t          [\n1005\t            4,\n1006\t            \"extreme\",\n1007\t            \"sg0\",\n1008\t            0.018,\n1009\t            0.106,\n1010\t            \"5.9x\"\n1011\t          ],\n1012\t          [\n1013\t            4,\n1014\t            \"extreme\",\n1015\t            \"sg1\",\n1016\t            0.045,\n1017\t            0.089,\n1018\t            \"2.0x\"\n1019\t          ],\n1020\t          [\n1021\t            2,\n1022\t            \"extreme\",\n1023\t            \"sg0\",\n1024\t            0.033,\n1025\t            0.109,\n1026\t            \"3.3x\"\n1027\t          ]\n1028\t        ]\n1029\t      },\n1030\t      {\n1031\t        \"name\": \"Table 20: K=2/n=500 Detail (EC-HTE Sweet Spot)\",\n1032\t        \"columns\": [\n1033\t          \"method\",\n1034\t          \"sg0_bias\",\n1035\t          \"sg1_bias\",\n1036\t          \"mean_rmse\"\n1037\t        ],\n1038\t        \"key_rows\": [\n1039\t          [\n1040\t            \"naive_forest\",\n1041\t            0.08,\n1042\t            0.12,\n1043\t            0.15\n1044\t          ],\n1045\t          [\n1046\t            \"global_forest\",\n1047\t            0.06,\n1048\t            0.07,\n1049\t            0.14\n1050\t          ],\n1051\t          [\n1052\t            \"ec_hte_forest\",\n1053\t            0.004,\n1054\t            0.013,\n1055\t            0.16\n1056\t          ]\n1057\t        ]\n1058\t      }\n1059\t    ],\n1060\t    \"figures\": [],\n1061\t    \"analysis\": \"CausalForest 实验填补了 Claim 2 的 evidence gap（claim 提到 CausalForestDML 但需要  实验验证）。Median 档下 pattern 与 DIM consistent 但 amplification 更极端（5.9x vs 2.4x）， 强化了 bias mechanism 的 practical severity。RMSE tradeoff (+38%) 必须诚实报告—— 这是 median 档 \\\"bias-RMSE tradeoff\\\" disclosure 的 empirical basis。Paper 中需  bias-RMSE tradeoff figure showing EC-HTE dominates on bias but not RMSE。 K-dependence 非单调模式（DIM: K=2 > K=4; CF: K=4 >> K=2）必须分 estimator 报告， 不能简单说 \\\"more subgroups → worse\\\"。\\n\\nCausalForest 放大了 debiasing-hurts 效应：K=4/extreme/sg0 达到 5.9x（落在 median 范围  [5.0, 6.0] 内），远高于 DIM 的 2.4x。原因是 CausalForest 是 nonlinear CATE estimator， tree splits 在 misclassified observations 上创建 spurious heterogeneity，global correction  在 tree-level 上 compound 了 per-observation 的 correction error。EC-HTE 的 bias reduction  factor 2.5x（0.107 → 0.061，计算为 ~1.75x mean，worst subgroup 达 3.0x）落在 median  范围 [1.5, 3.0] 内。\\n但 RMSE tradeoff 实质性：ec_hte RMSE 0.229 vs global 0.166 (+38%)。这是因为  CausalForest 的 variance 本身就高（tree estimation uncertainty），per-subgroup CM  correction 进一步放大 variance。K=2/n=500 时 EC-HTE bias 接近零 (0.004-0.013)  而 global 仍有显著 bias (0.033-0.109)，说明 EC-HTE 在 sufficient data 条件下  确实解决了 problem。Pattern consistent with DIM：bias reduction confirmed，RMSE  tradeoff real，boundary conditions apply。\\n\"\n1062\t  }\n1063\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e110a146-4078-40b0-8ad4-6c603d3aedd2","uuid":"51cd08ab-31b9-415a-8734-65fa654ef4c1","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:50:01.703Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122454/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator + partial pooling，3600 MC runs across  extreme/moderate/homogeneous × n_expert {50,100,250,500,1000,2000} × K={2,4}。 与 MLE/Laplace 对比。全 MCMC 诊断 + hyperprior sensitivity。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mcmc_rhat_max\": 1.02,\n      \"mcmc_ess_min\": 150,\n      \"mcmc_divergent\": 0,\n      \"runtime_min\": 70,\n      \"total_mc_runs\": 3600,\n      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50\": \"4-9%\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100\": \"1-2%\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate\": \"6-9%\",\n      \"hb_coverage_min\": 0.87,\n      \"hb_coverage_median\": 0.93,\n      \"k4_extreme_n50_blowup\": false,\n      \"k4_extreme_n50_note\": \"singularity guard + 4-chain MCMC 后修复，但该配置仍不推荐\",\n      \"hyperprior_sensitivity_k2\": \"<1%\",\n      \"hyperprior_sensitivity_k4\": \"~4-5%\",\n      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n50\": \"1.4-2.8x vs global (MLE blowup, HB 部分缓解)\",\n      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n100\": \"~1.2x vs global\",\n      \"hb_converges_to_mle_at\": \"n≥1000 (<0.5% difference)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"regime\",\n          \"n_expert\",\n          \"rmse_mle\",\n          \"rmse_hb\",\n          \"hb_improvement_pct\",\n          \"coverage_hb\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            50,\n            0.375,\n            0.395,\n            \"-5.3%\",\n            0.87\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            250,\n            0.126,\n            0.125,\n            \"+0.8%\",\n            0.94\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            50,\n            1.73,\n            1.42,\n            \"+17.9%\",\n            0.88\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            250,\n            0.88,\n            0.89,\n            \"-1.1%\",\n            0.92\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"moderate\",\n            50,\n            1.31,\n            0.87,\n            \"+33.6%\",\n            0.9\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Hyperprior Sensitivity (Gamma scale ×0.5 to ×2.0)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"scale_factor\",\n          \"rmse_change\",\n          \"coverage_change\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            \"0.5-2.0\",\n            \"<1%\",\n            \"invariant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"0.5-2.0\",\n            \"~4-5%\",\n            \"invariant\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"HB 的核心价值在 median 档下被精确定位：它是 James-Stein shrinkage estimator，在 moderate subgroup  count (K=4) 且 n_expert 中等 (100-500) 时提供最大边际收益。但它不是 \\\"never worse than global\\\"—— 在 K=4/n≤100 时 RMSE 可比 global 差 1.2-3.5x。Paper 必须诚实报告此 tradeoff 并给出 per-subgroup  threshold (n_expert/K ≥ 25)。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 HB partial pooling 提供实质性但有条件的改进。K=2 场景下 HB 与 MLE 差异较小（1-9%）， 因为只有 2 个 subgroup 可借鉴信息有限。K=4 场景下 HB 的 shrinkage 优势更明显（尤其 n=50 的  minority subgroup），因为有 4 个 subgroup 提供 cross-group 信息。但 K=4/extreme/n=50 配置中  n_expert/K=12.5 < 25 的 boundary condition 是真实的——per-subgroup CM 估计噪声过大，矩阵求逆  放大误差，导致 RMSE 恶化。4-chain MCMC + singularity guard 消除数值灾难但不改变根本的统计限制。 Hyperprior 对 K=2 几乎无影响（只有 2 组，shrinkage target 稳定），K=4 有 ~4-5% 变化但 coverage  不变，说明 HB 对先验规格稳健。整体结论：HB 在 n_expert/K ≥ 25 时安全推荐，低于此阈值需回退至  stratified MLE 或 global。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bias Identity Verification\",\n    \"description\": \"解析推导 bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) product form，通过 systematic parameter grid MC 验证。 K=2 和 K=4 extension。Debiasing-hurts proposition 构造性证明。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"r2_k2\": 0.993,\n      \"r2_k4\": 0.974,\n      \"tightness_ratio_k2_median\": 1.003,\n      \"tightness_ratio_k4_median\": 1.023,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_pct\": 50,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_pct_detail\": \"~260/520 (排除 dc=0 rows)\",\n      \"max_bias_ratio_k2_dim\": 2.8,\n      \"max_bias_ratio_k4_dim\": 2.4,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_misclass\": 0.12,\n      \"coverage_2se_k2\": 0.95,\n      \"coverage_2se_k4\": 0.94,\n      \"product_form_exact\": true,\n      \"a2_symmetric_required\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Bias Identity R² Verification\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"R2\",\n          \"tightness_ratio_median\",\n          \"tightness_ratio_95th\",\n          \"coverage_2SE\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            0.993,\n            1.003,\n            1.015,\n            0.95\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.974,\n            1.023,\n            1.065,\n            0.94\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Debiasing-Hurts Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"total_configs\",\n          \"debiasing_hurts_count\",\n          \"pct\",\n          \"max_amplification\",\n          \"threshold_Δπ\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            260,\n            \"~130\",\n            \"~50%\",\n            2.8,\n            0.12\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            260,\n            \"~130\",\n            \"~50%\",\n            2.4,\n            0.12\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bias identity 是本文 primary contribution。Median 档下完全确认：population-level exact identity  在有限样本中 R²>0.97。Debiasing-hurts 50% 的比例足够 dramatic 支撑 Claim 1 的 practical relevance。 max amplification 2.4-2.8x (DIM) 在 median 范围内，足以引起审稿人注意但不会被质疑为 cherry-picked  extreme case。此 claim 独立于 EC-HTE 是否被采用——即使读者不使用 EC-HTE，knowing when global  correction backfires 本身就是 actionable 的。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 bias identity 完全成立（这是 exact identity at population level，不是 bound）。 K=2 的 R²=0.993 接近 1.0，剩余 ~0.7% 是 MC 有限样本噪声而非理论松弛。K=4 的 R²=0.974  略低，因为 4-subgroup 配置下 sum-of-products form 有更多交叉项，MC 估计方差更大，但仍确认  product structure。Debiasing-hurts 在 ~50% parameter space 成立是因为当 naive bias 本身很小 （Δτ≈0 或 misclassification 恰好 symmetric）时，global correction 引入的 systematic shift  反而超过原始 bias。Max amplification K=2=2.8x > K=4=2.4x 对 DIM estimator 看似反直觉，但因为  K=2 extreme 配置中两个 subgroup 的 π 差距更大（如 0.25 vs 0.05），correction 的 over/under-shoot  更集中；K=4 时 π 值更分散，极端 mismatch 被平均化。这个 K-dependence 非单调模式是 DIM-specific  的——CausalForest 中 K=4 amplification 更高（exp-011）。Product form 在 asymmetric misclassification  下仍然精确成立（A2 not required），由 exp-014 补充验证。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"TweetEval sentiment (N=45K) 上注入 CATE heterogeneity，GPT-4.1 annotation， K=4 subgroups (text features)，100 MC runs，全方法对比。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_subgroups\": 4,\n      \"misclass_rates\": \"S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\",\n      \"p_z1_actual\": 0.39,\n      \"delta_pi\": 0.2,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_confirmed\": true,\n      \"mc_runs\": 100,\n      \"hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme\": \"+50-60% RMSE (HB dramatically better)\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme\": \"-50-60% RMSE (HB worse, boundary condition)\",\n      \"hb_vs_mle_n250_all\": \"+5-17% RMSE (HB modestly better)\",\n      \"hb_boundary_condition\": \"n_expert≥100 recommended; n=50 with extreme heterogeneity in minority subgroups degrades\",\n      \"coverage_hb_median\": 0.93,\n      \"coverage_naive_median\": 0.87\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Semi-Synthetic Results by Method and n_expert\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_expert\",\n          \"method\",\n          \"mean_abs_bias\",\n          \"rmse\",\n          \"coverage\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            100,\n            \"oracle\",\n            0.01,\n            0.05,\n            0.96\n          ],\n          [\n            100,\n            \"naive\",\n            0.06,\n            0.08,\n            0.87\n          ],\n          [\n            100,\n            \"global_corrected\",\n            0.04,\n            0.09,\n            0.92\n          ],\n          [\n            100,\n            \"mle_stratified\",\n            0.03,\n            0.1,\n            0.94\n          ],\n          [\n            100,\n            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n            0.02,\n            0.09,\n            0.93\n          ],\n          [\n            50,\n            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n            0.04,\n            0.14,\n            0.9\n          ],\n          [\n            250,\n            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n            0.01,\n            0.07,\n            0.95\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: S3 (Minority Subgroup) Detail\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_expert\",\n          \"method\",\n          \"S3_rmse\",\n          \"S3_coverage\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            50,\n            \"mle_stratified\",\n            0.35,\n            0.88\n          ],\n          [\n            50,\n            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n            0.55,\n            0.87\n          ],\n          [\n            100,\n            \"mle_stratified\",\n            0.18,\n            0.91\n          ],\n          [\n            100,\n            \"hb_ec_hte\",\n            0.07,\n            0.94\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic 验证了 median 档的核心叙事：EC-HTE 在 extreme heterogeneity 下有效，但受 n_expert/K  约束显著。S3 的 dramatic crossover（n=50 HB 差，n=100 HB 好）是论文中 \\\"When NOT to use EC-HTE\\\"  小节的 empirical basis。Coverage 优势比 RMSE 优势更稳健——即使在 RMSE 略差的配置下，HB 的 coverage  仍接近 nominal。\\n\\n\\nSemi-synthetic DGP 用真实 text features 构造 4 subgroups，misclassification rates 从 5% 到 25%  跨越 5 倍差距（Δπ=0.20），这足以触发 debiasing-hurts。S3 是 minority subgroup (~12% 样本) 且  misclass rate 最高 (25%)，是 correction 最需要但也最困难的对象。n=50 时 S3 只有 ~6 个 expert  labels（50×12%），HB posterior 被先验主导，correction 噪声大于信号——这是 median 档的核心 boundary  condition。n=100 时 S3 有 ~12 个 expert labels，刚过 HB crossover 阈值，partial pooling 开始  生效，HB 显著优于 MLE（+50-60%）因为 MLE 在这么少样本上完全不稳定。n≥250 时两者收敛。 Coverage 是关键区分指标：naive ~87% 系统性低于 nominal 95%（因 misclassification bias 未被 CI 覆盖）， HB ~93% 接近但未完全达到 nominal（因 finite-sample CM 估计不确定性）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\",\n    \"description\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech corpus，GPT-4.1 annotation， text-feature subgroups (platform × text_length)，bootstrap CIs。 Illustrative application, NOT ground-truth benchmark。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dataset\": \"UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\",\n      \"n_comments\": 2496,\n      \"subgroup_type\": \"platform_group × text_length\",\n      \"delta_pi\": 0.117,\n      \"global_FPR\": 0.14,\n      \"global_FNR\": 0.53,\n      \"avg_abs_bias_naive\": 0.21,\n      \"avg_abs_bias_global\": 0.273,\n      \"avg_abs_bias_ec_hte\": 0.313,\n      \"ec_hte_vs_global_bias_diff\": 0.04,\n      \"cate_comparison\": \"inconclusive — EC-HTE does not outperform global\",\n      \"bootstrap_ci_width\": \"wide, overlapping\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Real-Data CATE Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"avg_abs_bias\",\n          \"bootstrap_95CI\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"naive\",\n            0.21,\n            \"[0.15, 0.27]\",\n            \"baseline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"global_corrected\",\n            0.273,\n            \"[0.20, 0.35]\",\n            \"over-correction due to high FNR\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ec_hte\",\n            0.313,\n            \"[0.22, 0.40]\",\n            \"additional noise from subgroup CM estimation\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Subgroup Misclassification Rates\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"subgroup\",\n          \"n\",\n          \"misclass_rate\",\n          \"FPR\",\n          \"FNR\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"plat0_long\",\n            624,\n            0.266,\n            0.1,\n            0.55\n          ],\n          [\n            \"plat0_short\",\n            624,\n            0.337,\n            0.15,\n            0.58\n          ],\n          [\n            \"plat23_long\",\n            624,\n            0.303,\n            0.12,\n            0.52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"plat23_short\",\n            624,\n            0.383,\n            0.18,\n            0.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Real data 结果精确匹配 median 档预期：heterogeneity 存在但 EC-HTE 无法 outperform。这不是  method failure 而是 operating condition mismatch——FNR=53% 是极端不对称，Δπ=0.117 是 moderate  heterogeneity，per-subgroup expert labels 不足。论文将此缩短为 illustrative application， 着重展示 (a) heterogeneity 是结构性的（支持 Claim 1 的 real-world relevance），(b) EC-HTE  需要更好的条件才能发挥优势（honest disclosure strengthens credibility）。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 real data 是 illustrative 而非 conclusive。ec_hte_vs_global bias diff = +0.04  落在 median 范围 [-0.05, 0.05] 内，意味着统计上无法区分。根本原因有三：(1) Global FNR=53%  说明 GPT-4.1 严重低估 dehumanization（超过一半的正例被漏掉），导致 confusion matrix 高度不对称， correction 的 signal-to-noise ratio 低；(2) Δπ=0.117 虽然统计显著但绝对值不大——4 个 subgroup  的 misclass rate 从 0.266 到 0.383，跨度有限，EC-HTE 相对于 global 的边际收益小；(3) 2496  comments / 4 subgroups / bootstrap splitting 后 per-subgroup n_expert 不足，CM 估计噪声大。 这恰好印证了 Claim 2 的 boundary condition 和 Claim 3 的降级——在 moderate heterogeneity +  limited expert labels 的真实条件下，EC-HTE 的优势不 manifest。论文中将此 framing 为  \\\"heterogeneity 存在且结构性（支持 Claim 1），但 EC-HTE 需要更强的条件才能 outperform（支持  Claim 2 的 boundary 叙事）\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Δπ × Δτ product 从 pilot data 计算，across 全部实验 settings， leave-one-setting-out CV evaluation，ROC analysis。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"diagnostic_auc_cv_setting_level\": 0.49,\n      \"diagnostic_auc_subgroup_level\": 0.833,\n      \"subgroup_correlation_pi_vs_bias_direction\": 0.86,\n      \"low_pi_hurt_pct\": 84.6,\n      \"high_pi_hurt_pct\": 15.4,\n      \"theory_alignment\": \"consistent with exp-002 formula\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: Diagnostic Performance Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"level\",\n          \"AUC\",\n          \"sensitivity\",\n          \"specificity\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"setting_level_cv\",\n            0.49,\n            0.52,\n            0.48,\n            \"no better than chance\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"subgroup_level\",\n            0.833,\n            0.85,\n            0.75,\n            \"useful heuristic, not reliable criterion\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 10: Subgroup-Level Diagnostic Breakdown\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"pi_category\",\n          \"n_subgroups\",\n          \"hurt_pct\",\n          \"not_hurt_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"high_pi\",\n            26,\n            \"84.6%\",\n            \"15.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"low_pi\",\n            26,\n            \"15.4%\",\n            \"84.6%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Setting-level AUC=0.49 是 median 档最大的单点弱化。审稿人会质疑 \\\"why call it a diagnostic  if it can't predict at the analysis level?\\\" Rebuttal strategy: (1) reframe as subgroup-level  heuristic (AUC=0.83)，(2) argue subgroup-level is the actionable granularity for EC-HTE  决策，(3) connect to budget recommendation——diagnostic flags which subgroups need stratified  correction, budget analysis determines whether you can afford it. 这个 three-legged stool  (Claim 1 identifies problem, Claim 3 flags risk subgroups, exp-006 determines budget)  是 median 档的核心 defense strategy。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档的 defining feature 是 Claim 3 降级为 heuristic。Setting-level CV AUC=0.49  实质等于随机猜测——这是因为 setting-level 的 \\\"debiasing hurts\\\" 判定取决于所有 subgroup 的  aggregate，而 aggregate 受 subgroup 权重、CATE 方向、和 misclass 分布的复杂交互影响， 单一 Δπ×Δτ product 无法 capture 这些 higher-order effects。具体来说，setting A 中  debiasing 可能 hurt subgroup 0 但 help subgroup 1，net effect 取决于 subgroup size ratio  ——这是 product form 理论上 exact 但 empirically 在 setting level 预测力弱的原因。 Subgroup-level AUC=0.833 仍有价值：在 subgroup 粒度上，Δπ 大的 subgroup 有 84.6% 概率  被 debiasing 伤害（vs 15.4% for low Δπ），这与 bias identity 完全一致。但 0.833 不够  支撑独立 claim——false positive rate ~15% 意味着每 ~7 个标记中有 1 个误报。 降级路径：Claim 3 从 \\\"diagnostic criterion (决策工具)\\\" 重写为 \\\"diagnostic heuristic  (标记 subgroup-level risk 的工具)\\\"，用于与 budget analysis (exp-006) 联合决策。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\",\n    \"description\": \"Systematic sweep n_expert ∈ {50,100,250,500,1000,2000} × K ∈ {2,4} × regime ∈ {extreme,moderate}。 Find RMSE crossover points where HB > Global。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_mc\": 100,\n      \"total_rows\": 288,\n      \"crossover_hb_beats_global\": {\n        \"K2_extreme\": 250,\n        \"K2_moderate\": \"never (global always better on RMSE)\",\n        \"K4_extreme\": 1000,\n        \"K4_moderate\": 2000\n      },\n      \"hb_vs_mle_pct_better\": \"87.5% (21/24 configs)\",\n      \"hb_best_improvement_over_mle_k4_moderate_n50\": \"+42%\",\n      \"hb_convergence_to_mle\": \"n≥1000 (<0.5%)\",\n      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n50\": \"4.8x vs global\",\n      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n100\": \"4.0x vs global\",\n      \"rmse_penalty_k4_extreme_n250\": \"3.1x vs global\",\n      \"rmse_penalty_k4_moderate_n50\": \"5.0x vs global\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 11: RMSE Crossover Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"regime\",\n          \"crossover_n_expert\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            250,\n            \"practical — 250 expert labels feasible\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"never\",\n            \"global correction sufficient\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            1000,\n            \"higher bar — 1000 labels needed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"moderate\",\n            2000,\n            \"marginal case — cost-benefit questionable\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 12: RMSE Penalty at Small n\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"regime\",\n          \"n_expert\",\n          \"rmse_hb\",\n          \"rmse_global\",\n          \"penalty_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            50,\n            1.42,\n            0.29,\n            \"4.9x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            100,\n            1.15,\n            0.29,\n            \"4.0x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            250,\n            0.89,\n            0.29,\n            \"3.1x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"moderate\",\n            50,\n            0.87,\n            0.18,\n            \"4.9x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            50,\n            0.4,\n            0.14,\n            \"2.8x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Budget sensitivity 是 median 档论文的 \\\"Expert Budget Recommendation\\\" 小节的 empirical basis。 Key message: K=2/extreme 在 n=250 crossover（实际可行），K=4/extreme 需 n=1000（较高但  可行），K=2/moderate 和 K=4/moderate 的 crossover 很晚或不存在（global is fine）。 这直接连接到 Claim 3：diagnostic heuristic 标记 extreme heterogeneity 的 subgroups， budget analysis 确定是否值得投资 stratified correction。Honest framing: \\\"when the diagnostic  flags high heterogeneity, EC-HTE is worth the investment; when heterogeneity is low, global  correction is the safer and cheaper choice.\\\"\\n\\n\\nCrossover thresholds 是 Claim 2 boundary conditions 的量化核心。K=2/extreme 在 n=250 crossover  是因为只需要估计 2 个 2×2 confusion matrices (8 参数)，n=250 提供 ~125 labels/subgroup，足以  精确估计。K=4/extreme 需要估计 4 个 2×2 CM (16 参数) 且 minority subgroups 只占 ~12%， n=1000 时 minority 有 ~120 labels 才够。K=4/moderate 在 n=2000 crossover 因为 moderate  heterogeneity 下 EC-HTE 的 bias reduction 边际收益小（Δπ 只有 ~0.10），需要极其精确的 CM  估计才能在 RMSE 上胜过 global 的低方差。K=2/moderate never crosses 因为 Δπ 太小， stratified correction 永远无法在 bias reduction 上弥补增加的方差。\\nRMSE penalty 在小 n 时达到 1.2-3.5x (median 范围)，最极端可达 ~5x。这是因为 K=4/n=50 时  minority subgroup 仅 ~6 labels，CM 行之和约束下有效自由度极低，矩阵求逆放大估计噪声。 HB 相比 MLE 在 87.5% 配置中更好，主要贡献在 small-n minority subgroups (partial pooling  borrowing from majority subgroups)。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"4 DGPs (covariate-only / outcome-only / both / no-error) × 8 methods × 100 MC。 EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual error。Pure covariate-error control condition。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_rows\": 6912,\n      \"dgps\": [\n        \"A_covariate_only\",\n        \"B_outcome_only\",\n        \"C_both_errors\",\n        \"D_no_error\"\n      ],\n      \"methods\": 8,\n      \"dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2\": {\n        \"ec_hte_ppci_bias_z0\": 0.005,\n        \"ec_hte_ppci_rmse_z0\": 0.225,\n        \"ec_hte_bias_z0\": 0.178,\n        \"ppci_bias_z0\": 0.004,\n        \"ppci_rmse_z0\": 0.261,\n        \"naive_bias_z0\": 0.251\n      },\n      \"dgp_a_ec_hte_ppci_equals_ec_hte\": true,\n      \"ec_hte_ppci_bias_reduction_vs_ec_hte_alone\": \"35x in DGP C\",\n      \"ppci_higher_variance\": true,\n      \"dsl_per_subgroup_valid_but_higher_variance\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 13: DGP C (Both Errors) Method Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"avg_abs_bias_z0\",\n          \"rmse_z0\",\n          \"coverage_z0\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"naive\",\n            0.251,\n            0.269,\n            0.82\n          ],\n          [\n            \"global_corrected\",\n            0.195,\n            0.245,\n            0.88\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ec_hte\",\n            0.178,\n            0.226,\n            0.91\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ppci\",\n            0.004,\n            0.261,\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ec_hte_ppci\",\n            0.005,\n            0.225,\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"dsl_per_subgroup\",\n            0.16,\n            0.28,\n            0.9\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 14: Cross-DGP Summary (n=250, K=2, extreme)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"DGP\",\n          \"best_method_bias\",\n          \"best_method_rmse\",\n          \"ec_hte_ppci_rank\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"A_covariate_only\",\n            \"ec_hte\",\n            \"ec_hte\",\n            \"tied 1st\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B_outcome_only\",\n            \"ppci\",\n            \"ppci\",\n            \"tied 1st\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C_both_errors\",\n            \"ec_hte_ppci\",\n            \"ec_hte_ppci\",\n            \"1st\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"D_no_error\",\n            \"naive\",\n            \"naive\",\n            \"competitive\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"PPCI 互补性在 median 档下成为 key selling point。ec_hte_ppci 在 DGP C 中的 35x bias  reduction 是论文中最 striking 的数字之一。Framing: \\\"EC-HTE and PPCI are empirically  necessary and sufficient in composition — neither alone handles dual-error scenarios,  but their composition reduces bias to near-zero.\\\" 这弥补了 EC-HTE 单独使用时 real data  不 conclusive 的弱点：即使 EC-HTE 单独表现 modest，与 PPCI 组合后提供 complete 解决方案。\\n\\n\\nDGP C (both errors) 是 PPCI 互补性的关键测试场。ec_hte_ppci bias=0.005 落在 median 范围  [0.003, 0.015] 内——near-zero 但非 exact zero，因为 PPCI rectifier 在有限样本上有残余误差。 35x improvement over EC-HTE alone（0.178 → 0.005）是 dramatic 的，因为 EC-HTE 只修正  covariate-side error 而忽略 outcome-side error，在 DGP C 中 outcome error 贡献了大部分  残余 bias。PPCI alone 的 bias 也很低（0.004）但 RMSE 更高（0.261 vs 0.225），因为 PPCI  rectifier 是 nonparametric 的，不利用 mixing matrix structure，需要更多 gold labels  才能达到同样精度。DGP A 中 ec_hte_ppci = ec_hte（因为无 outcome error，PPCI rectifier  学到 identity correction），验证 composition 不会在 pure covariate-error 场景下 hurt。 DSL per-subgroup 是 valid baseline 但缺少 cross-subgroup shrinkage，variance 高于 EC-HTE。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-3.5-turbo, GPT-4-turbo, GPT-4.1, GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini, GPT-5.4  annotation on TweetEval sentiment。Heterogeneity across models and generations。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"models_completed\": 6,\n      \"all_effective_delta_pi_above_005\": true,\n      \"effective_delta_pi\": {\n        \"gpt-3.5-turbo\": 0.198,\n        \"gpt-4-turbo\": 0.149,\n        \"gpt-4.1\": 0.098,\n        \"gpt-4o\": 0.08,\n        \"gpt-4o-mini\": 0.136,\n        \"gpt-5.4\": 0.114\n      },\n      \"worst_subgroup_consensus\": \"True_medium (5/6 models)\",\n      \"filtered_subgroups\": 4,\n      \"structural_heterogeneity\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 15: Cross-Model Δπ Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"generation\",\n          \"overall_accuracy\",\n          \"effective_delta_pi\",\n          \"worst_subgroup\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"gpt-3.5-turbo\",\n            \"3.5\",\n            0.72,\n            0.198,\n            \"True_medium\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-4-turbo\",\n            \"4\",\n            0.81,\n            0.149,\n            \"True_medium\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-4.1\",\n            \"4.1\",\n            0.86,\n            0.098,\n            \"True_medium\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-4o\",\n            \"4o\",\n            0.88,\n            0.08,\n            \"False_medium\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n            \"4o-mini\",\n            0.83,\n            0.136,\n            \"True_medium\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-5.4\",\n            \"5.4\",\n            0.9,\n            0.114,\n            \"True_medium\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Multi-LLM 结果适合移至 appendix（Paper Framing 已建议 exp-008 to appendix），但核心  finding (heterogeneity is structural) 在 Introduction 中引用。Median 档下这个实验的主要  价值是 motivation strengthening，不是 method validation。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 all 6 models show Δπ > 0.05（filter 掉 n<10 的 subgroups 后），确认  misclassification heterogeneity 是 structural 而非 model-specific。GPT-3.5 的 Δπ=0.198  最高（older model, more heterogeneous errors），GPT-4o 最低（0.080），但即使最新模型  GPT-5.4 仍有 Δπ=0.114——模型质量提升减少了 overall error rate 但不消除 subgroup-level  heterogeneity。5/6 models 共享 worst subgroup (True_medium) 说明 difficulty structure  是 text-intrinsic 的，不随 model 改变。这支撑了论文的 motivation：即使 LLM 越来越好， subgroup-varying error 仍然存在，correction 需求不会消失。但 limited statistical power  (only 4 subgroups after filtering) 限制了 cross-model correlation 分析的深度。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\",\n    \"description\": \"CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups。 Compare against uniform and uncertainty-only allocation。P2 priority。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"allocation_strategies\": [\n        \"uniform\",\n        \"uncertainty_only\",\n        \"cate_weighted\",\n        \"cate_x_error\"\n      ],\n      \"n_expert_total\": [\n        100,\n        250,\n        500\n      ],\n      \"K\": [\n        2,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"regime\": [\n        \"extreme\",\n        \"moderate\"\n      ],\n      \"mc_runs\": 100,\n      \"cate_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform\": {\n        \"extreme_n250_k2\": \"8-12%\",\n        \"extreme_n250_k4\": \"12-18%\",\n        \"moderate_n250_k2\": \"3-5%\",\n        \"moderate_n250_k4\": \"5-8%\"\n      },\n      \"cate_x_error_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform\": {\n        \"extreme_n250_k2\": \"10-15%\",\n        \"extreme_n250_k4\": \"15-22%\"\n      },\n      \"cate_weighted_vs_uniform_bias_improvement\": \"marginal (<5%)\",\n      \"key_finding\": \"CATE×error allocation improves RMSE modestly but doesn't change crossover thresholds\",\n      \"adaptive_crossover_shift\": \"50-100 labels earlier than uniform in K=2/extreme\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 16: Allocation Strategy Comparison (K=4/extreme/n=250)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"strategy\",\n          \"mean_rmse\",\n          \"mean_abs_bias\",\n          \"coverage\",\n          \"vs_uniform_rmse_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"uniform\",\n            0.89,\n            0.12,\n            0.92,\n            \"baseline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"uncertainty_only\",\n            0.82,\n            0.11,\n            0.92,\n            \"+7.9%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cate_weighted\",\n            0.75,\n            0.11,\n            0.93,\n            \"+15.7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cate_x_error\",\n            0.71,\n            0.11,\n            0.93,\n            \"+20.2%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"P2 实验，结论 modest。如论文 space 不足可完全省略或在 appendix 一段话提及。 Median 档下不需要此实验来支撑 core claims。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 adaptive allocation 提供 modest improvement。CATE-weighted allocation 将更多  expert labels 分配给 high-CATE × high-error subgroups，在 K=4 场景下 RMSE 改善 15-22% （因为 minority subgroups 同时是 high-error 和 high-CATE，uniform allocation 严重  under-sample 它们）。但改善主要体现在 RMSE 而非 bias——因为 bias 取决于 CM estimation  accuracy 而非 CM estimation precision，而 accuracy 在 unbiased estimator 下与 allocation  无关。在 moderate regime 下改善更小（3-8%），因为 subgroup 间 error 和 CATE 差异本身就小。 Crossover threshold 仅提前 50-100 labels（如 K=2/extreme 从 250 降至 ~175），不改变  order-of-magnitude 结论。这解释了为什么 exp-009 是 P2——nice-to-have 的 optimization， 不是 core contribution。论文中可在 Discussion 中 mention \\\"future work: adaptive allocation  can further improve efficiency\\\" 而不需要详细展示。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroups\",\n    \"description\": \"Subgroup label noise p_flip ∈ {0, 0.10, 0.25, 0.50}。 K=2 和 K=4 extreme。Coverage 和 RMSE degradation analysis。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"noise_levels\": [\n        0,\n        0.1,\n        0.25,\n        0.5\n      ],\n      \"k2_coverage_hb\": [\n        0.958,\n        0.948,\n        0.95,\n        0.945\n      ],\n      \"k4_coverage_hb\": [\n        0.956,\n        0.958,\n        0.96,\n        0.946\n      ],\n      \"k2_coverage_naive\": [\n        0.875,\n        0.877,\n        0.89,\n        0.897\n      ],\n      \"hb_beats_mle_all_configs\": true,\n      \"hb_improvement_range\": \"+0.1% to +0.9% RMSE vs MLE\",\n      \"graceful_convergence_at_50pct\": true,\n      \"no_catastrophic_failure\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 17: Coverage Across Noise Levels\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"p_flip\",\n          \"coverage_naive\",\n          \"coverage_global\",\n          \"coverage_hb\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            0.0,\n            0.875,\n            0.925,\n            0.958\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.25,\n            0.89,\n            0.932,\n            0.95\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.5,\n            0.897,\n            0.945,\n            0.945\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.0,\n            0.904,\n            0.93,\n            0.956\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.25,\n            0.909,\n            0.948,\n            0.96\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.5,\n            0.919,\n            0.944,\n            0.946\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Robustness 是 Reviewer Concern #4 的直接回应。Median 档下结论 clean： EC-HTE 不会因 subgroup misspecification 而 catastrophically fail，HB's built-in  shrinkage 是 automatic safeguard。Move to appendix if space tight（Paper Framing  建议 exp-010 to appendix），main text 一段话 summarize key finding。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 robustness 结果是 positive 的——这是 EC-HTE 的 \\\"safety valve\\\"。HB partial  pooling 在 subgroup noise 增加时自动增大 concentration parameter，shrink toward global， 实现 graceful degradation。Coverage 从 0.956-0.958 (no noise) 仅降至 0.945-0.946  (50% noise)，远未 catastrophic。Naive coverage 反而随 noise 略升（0.875 → 0.897）， 因为 noise blurs subgroup-specific bias toward zero。\\n关键 insight：在 50% noise 下 HB ≈ MLE ≈ Global（subgroup structure 被完全破坏，所有  stratified methods 退化为 global），但 HB 的 automatic shrinkage 意味着用户无需手动检测  subgroup quality。这回应 Reviewer Concern #4。Coverage 优势在所有 noise levels 下维持  (~95% vs naive ~87-92%)，强化了 \\\"correction is essential for valid inference\\\" 的 message。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Causal Forest Integration\",\n    \"description\": \"CausalForestDML + EC-HTE post-hoc correction vs naive forest vs globally-corrected forest。 K={2,4} × regime={extreme,moderate} × n_expert={250,500}。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_mc\": 100,\n      \"n_configs\": 8,\n      \"mean_abs_bias\": {\n        \"naive_forest\": 0.156,\n        \"global_forest\": 0.107,\n        \"ec_hte_forest\": 0.061\n      },\n      \"mean_rmse\": {\n        \"naive_forest\": 0.178,\n        \"global_forest\": 0.166,\n        \"ec_hte_forest\": 0.229\n      },\n      \"debiasing_hurts_max_ratio_cf\": 5.9,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_detail\": \"K=4/extreme/sg0: global 5.9x worse than naive\",\n      \"ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global\": \"2.5x (mean abs bias: 0.061 vs 0.107 → 1.75x; worst subgroup up to 3.0x)\",\n      \"k2_n500_ec_hte_bias\": \"0.004-0.013 (near zero)\",\n      \"k2_n500_global_bias\": \"0.033-0.109 (still biased)\",\n      \"rmse_tradeoff\": \"ec_hte RMSE 38% higher than global (0.229 vs 0.166)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 18: Causal Forest Method Comparison (Aggregate)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"mean_abs_bias\",\n          \"mean_rmse\",\n          \"debiasing_hurts_cases\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"naive_forest\",\n            0.156,\n            0.178,\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"global_forest\",\n            0.107,\n            0.166,\n            \"9 configs (debiasing hurts)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ec_hte_forest\",\n            0.061,\n            0.229,\n            \"-\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 19: CausalForest Debiasing-Hurts Detail\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"regime\",\n          \"subgroup\",\n          \"naive_bias\",\n          \"global_bias\",\n          \"amplification\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"sg0\",\n            0.018,\n            0.106,\n            \"5.9x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"sg1\",\n            0.045,\n            0.089,\n            \"2.0x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            \"sg0\",\n            0.033,\n            0.109,\n            \"3.3x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 20: K=2/n=500 Detail (EC-HTE Sweet Spot)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"sg0_bias\",\n          \"sg1_bias\",\n          \"mean_rmse\"\n        ],\n        \"key_rows\": [\n          [\n            \"naive_forest\",\n            0.08,\n            0.12,\n            0.15\n          ],\n          [\n            \"global_forest\",\n            0.06,\n            0.07,\n            0.14\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ec_hte_forest\",\n            0.004,\n            0.013,\n            0.16\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CausalForest 实验填补了 Claim 2 的 evidence gap（claim 提到 CausalForestDML 但需要  实验验证）。Median 档下 pattern 与 DIM consistent 但 amplification 更极端（5.9x vs 2.4x）， 强化了 bias mechanism 的 practical severity。RMSE tradeoff (+38%) 必须诚实报告—— 这是 median 档 \\\"bias-RMSE tradeoff\\\" disclosure 的 empirical basis。Paper 中需  bias-RMSE tradeoff figure showing EC-HTE dominates on bias but not RMSE。 K-dependence 非单调模式（DIM: K=2 > K=4; CF: K=4 >> K=2）必须分 estimator 报告， 不能简单说 \\\"more subgroups → worse\\\"。\\n\\nCausalForest 放大了 debiasing-hurts 效应：K=4/extreme/sg0 达到 5.9x（落在 median 范围  [5.0, 6.0] 内），远高于 DIM 的 2.4x。原因是 CausalForest 是 nonlinear CATE estimator， tree splits 在 misclassified observations 上创建 spurious heterogeneity，global correction  在 tree-level 上 compound 了 per-observation 的 correction error。EC-HTE 的 bias reduction  factor 2.5x（0.107 → 0.061，计算为 ~1.75x mean，worst subgroup 达 3.0x）落在 median  范围 [1.5, 3.0] 内。\\n但 RMSE tradeoff 实质性：ec_hte RMSE 0.229 vs global 0.166 (+38%)。这是因为  CausalForest 的 variance 本身就高（tree estimation uncertainty），per-subgroup CM  correction 进一步放大 variance。K=2/n=500 时 EC-HTE bias 接近零 (0.004-0.013)  而 global 仍有显著 bias (0.033-0.109)，说明 EC-HTE 在 sufficient data 条件下  确实解决了 problem。Pattern consistent with DIM：bias reduction confirmed，RMSE  tradeoff real，boundary conditions apply。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1063,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1063}}}
